// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/show-an-icon.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeShowAnIcon(path: "/recipes/show-an-icon", title: "Show an icon — Recipes", description: "Draw one of the 83 built-in icons inline with Icon(\"name\"), size and colour it with flags, and use one on a button or a sidebar item.") {
    RecipeShell("Show an icon", summary: "Draw an icon with `Icon(\"name\")`: one of 83 built-in SVG icons, drawn inline in the current text colour, so it follows the theme. Use it beside text, on an icon-only button or in a sidebar.  This page shows icons on their own, on an icon-only button, and in a sidebar:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "the-built-in-icons", label: "The built-in icons"), Anchor(id: "use-an-icon-that-is-not-built-in", label: "Use an icon that is not built in"), Anchor(id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add a picture, sized for every screen", to: "/recipes/add-a-picture"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Add video and audio", to: "/recipes/video-and-audio"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Show a carousel", to: "/recipes/show-a-carousel")], source: "md-docs/recipes/show-an-icon.md", how: true, hasVariations: false) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** nothing besides the page. It claims `/`: paste it into a new project, or replace the starter's `src/pages/Home.wf` with it.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Inbox(path: "/", title: "Inbox", description: "Messages, with icons.") {
    Heading("Inbox").h1
    Row(gap: .sm) {
        Icon("mail")
        Icon("bell").lg.primary
        IconButton(icon: "close", label: "Close the inbox")
    }
    Sidebar {
        Sidebar.Item(to: "/", icon: "home") { Text("Home") }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("- `Icon(\"mail\")` draws the icon named `mail`. The `.sm` and `.lg` flags size it, and a tone flag such as `.primary` colours it.\n- `IconButton` is a button that shows only an icon. Its `label:` is its accessible name for screen readers, and also its tooltip unless you give it a `title:`.\n- `Sidebar.Item` takes an `icon:` too.")

        Heading("The built-in icons", id: "the-built-in-icons").h2

        Markdown("These are the 83 built-in icons:\n\n- **General**: `home`, `menu`, `search`, `close`, `user`, `settings`, `check`, `plus`, `minus`, `edit`, `trash`, `star`, `heart`, `mail`, `bell`, `download`, `upload`, `eye`, `link`, `calendar`, `filter`, `info`, `warning`, `arrow-left`, `arrow-right`, `chevron-down`, `chevron-right`, `chevron-left`, `logout`, `copy`, `sun`, `moon`.\n- **For an editor or a tool**: `folder`, `folder-plus`, `folder-off`, `file`, `file-plus`, `refresh`, `alert-circle`, `clock`, `dot`, `diff`, `book`, `git-pull-request`, `pin`, `git-branch`, `more-horizontal`, `window-minimize`, `window-maximize`, `outline`, `help-circle`, `collapse-all`, `locate`, `chevron-up`, `globe`, `external-link`, `panel-down`, `panel-up`, `code`, `monitor`, `git-commit`, `play`, `layers`, `insert`, `grid`, `list`, `square`, `pill`, `image`, `sparkle`, `lock`, `type`, `pointer`, `reach`, `frame`, `line`, `pipette`, `comment`, `hand`, `zoom`, `ruler`, `eye-off`, `unlock`.\n\nA name that is not in the list draws as the word itself, and the compiler warns with `V08`.")

        Callout("The build keeps only the glyphs your program names. If an icon's name arrives at run time, set `\"build\": \{ \"runtime\": \"full\" \}` so every glyph ships.", kind: .important)

        Heading("Use an icon that is not built in", id: "use-an-icon-that-is-not-built-in").h2

        Markdown("For an icon that is not built in, put an SVG file in `public/` and show it with `Image(src: \"/icons/rocket.svg\", alt: \"\")`.")

        Heading("Troubleshooting", id: "troubleshooting").h2

        Table(caption: "Troubleshooting") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("What you see").header
                    Table.Cell("Why, and what to do").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("An icon shows as a word")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The name is not one of the built-in icons (`V08`), or it arrives at run time and the build left its glyph out. Use a listed name, or set `build.runtime` to `\"full\"`") }
                }
            }
        }

    }
}
